meta {
  name: List Specific Device for given user
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/devices/{{deviceid}}?personId={{personid}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  personId: {{personid}}
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Gets the details of one specific device, scoped to a specific user — the "Get Device Details"
  endpoint with an added `personId` filter.

  **Parameters**
  - `deviceId` (path) — the ID of the device to look up. Bound to `{{deviceid}}`, an example
    workspace desk phone.
  - `personId` (query) — the person the device should belong to. Bound to `{{personid}}`.

  **Usage**: This request will give you the details of a specific device associated with a specific
  user. Use "List Devices" or "Get Devices For User" first to find a `deviceId`, then use this to
  drill into that one device's full detail record.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/devices/get-device-details

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
